-- ASSUME keyword examples

-- Assuming plain facts

-- Each name says what kind of thing it is, and carries no value
ASSUME `is employed` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `annual income` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `applicant name` IS A STRING

-- Assuming a rule defined elsewhere

-- One input, one answer
ASSUME `calculate tax` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- The assumed rule can be used like any other
DECIDE `tax on income` IS `calculate tax` `annual income`

-- Reading assumed names in a decision

ASSUME age IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `has valid license` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Combine assumed facts in one rule
DECIDE `can drive` IS
  age >= 16 AND `has valid license`

-- Asking about a rule that reads assumed names

-- #CHECK reports the kind of answer without working one out
#CHECK `can drive`

-- A longer example: an eligibility check

ASSUME `applicant age` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `years of residence` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `has criminal record` IS A BOOLEAN

DECIDE `is eligible for benefit` IS
      `applicant age` >= 21
  AND `years of residence` >= 5
  AND NOT `has criminal record`

#CHECK `is eligible for benefit`

-- Binding Assumed Values

-- No directive binds an ASSUME inside a file; values arrive at deployment.
-- To test in the file, make the input a GIVEN parameter and supply it by name.

GIVEN `applicant age for test` IS A NUMBER
DECIDE `is adult` IF `applicant age for test` >= 18

#EVAL `is adult` WITH `applicant age for test` IS 25
#ASSERT `is adult` WITH `applicant age for test` IS 25

-- Where a term ASSUME goes now: a GIVEN under the section heading

-- The GIVEN is indented past the § of the heading, so it belongs to the
-- section, and every rule in the section reads it without re-declaring it.
-- It behaves exactly as the ASSUMEs above do: assumed until supplied.

§ `Driving eligibility`
    GIVEN `driver age` IS A NUMBER
          `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN

DECIDE `may drive alone` IS
  `driver age` >= 18 AND `holds a valid licence`

DECIDE `may drive supervised` IS
  `driver age` >= 16 AND `holds a valid licence`

#CHECK `may drive alone`
#CHECK `may drive supervised`
